note Where every node on the canvas ends up. The layout is a forest of compact subtrees, recomputed from scratch every frame until the reader drags a node. Horizontally a node's column is its depth in the path tree, or one hop out from whatever expansion revealed it, and the columns are placed outward from column 0 so the root of the path never moves. Vertically each node owns a block as tall as itself or as the stack of its children's blocks, whichever is more, and centres in it; sibling blocks never interleave, so a wide subtree only pushes its own siblings around. A final sweep separates the rare collisions between different subtrees that land in the same column.

